findings.body:
Every other predicate in this PR passes `escape="\\"`, but the "not contains" branch does not. It works today only because PostgreSQL and MySQL default to backslash as the LIKE escape. Any other backend, or a future change to the default, would turn this into a wildcard match.

::diff{file="api/core/rag/retrieval/dataset_retrieval.py" lines="1205-1207"}

Add `escape="\\"` to the `notlike` call so all branches are consistent.

The f-string `ESCAPE '\\\\'` in Python produces `ESCAPE '\\'` in the generated SQL. Standard SQL requires the ESCAPE value to be a single character, and `'\\'` is two characters. The generated SQL may only be valid if ClickZetta treats backslash as a string-literal escape. This is not verified in the PR or its tests.

::diff{file="api/core/rag/datasource/vdb/clickzetta/clickzetta_vector.py" lines="987-991"}

Verify the ClickZetta grammar. If backslash is a single-character escape there, the literal should be `'\\'` in the generated SQL. Add a ClickZetta test that exercises `%` and `_` in a query.

`escapedPattern` in the new helper is camelCase, but the rest of the module and the codebase use snake_case, and the function parameter is `pattern`. This is minor, but it is the first thing a reviewer will see in the new shared utility.

::diff{file="api/libs/helper.py" lines="63-65"}

Rename to `escaped_pattern`, or return the chained expression directly.
